# 81. CORE RULES

```text
RULE 01
Every character must have a unique Character_ID.

RULE 02
Family_ID represents the actual Family Entity.

RULE 03
Family Name may be duplicated.

RULE 04
⭐1 has 10% Noble Chance.

RULE 05
⭐2 has 10% Noble Chance.

RULE 06
⭐3 has 40% Noble Chance.

RULE 07
⭐4 has 40% Noble Chance.

RULE 08
⭐5 has 40% Noble Chance.

RULE 09
Noble Chance is calculated independently
for every generated character.

RULE 10
Noble Chance does not guarantee a Noble result.

RULE 11
Failed Noble RNG produces a Non-Noble background.

RULE 12
Successful Noble RNG creates a Family Entity.

RULE 13
Royal and Imperial characters require
appropriate world-building conditions.

RULE 14
Family_ID remains attached to the Character_ID.

RULE 15
Star Up does not reroll Family.

RULE 16
Star Up does not reroll Noble Second Name.

RULE 17
Star Up does not reroll Noble Skill.

RULE 18
Family Name does not determine combat power.

RULE 19
One Family_ID may contain multiple characters.

RULE 20
Family Entity may contain Bloodline data.

RULE 21
Every Noble character receives at least
one Noble Skill.

RULE 22
Noble Skill must be selected according to
Family, Bloodline, House Rank, Race, and Core World Build.

RULE 23
Non-Noble characters do not receive
Noble Second Name or Noble Skill.

RULE 24
Noble Skill may be inherited through
Family Tree and Bloodline.

RULE 25
Noble Skill must have a unique Noble_Skill_ID.

RULE 26
Family data must be stored persistently
in the Database System.

RULE 27
Noble RNG configuration must be adjustable
through the Economy/Global Configuration System
without changing Character Entity structure.

RULE 28
Noble Skill configuration must be adjustable
without changing Character_ID or Family_ID.

RULE 29
Noble Second Name must remain connected
to a valid Family_ID or Bloodline_ID.

RULE 30
Core World Build is the primary reference
for Noble Skill naming and design.
```

